<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ābrăham</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ābram</span></b> , indecl. or
			ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Abraham</i> (eccl.
			Lat.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence
			derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Abrāhămĭdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>a descendant of
				Abraham</i> (eccl. Lat.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Abrāhămēus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Abrāmēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>belonging
				to Abraham</i> (eccl. Lat.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
